# Build output. The .hex is generated too — unlike tb/fw_smoke.hex, which is
# hand-encoded precisely so the CPU testbench needs no toolchain.
*.o
*.d
*.elf
*.hex
*.map

# The requant table adder_export.py / ../host/run_adder.py derive from a real
# checkpoint and build adder.c against. Generated per run; the tracked table is
# adder_rq.h, whose words are tuned for the synthetic test operands instead.
adder_rq_ckpt.h
